# Safety-critical paths — the controls that govern the autonomous agent itself. A change to any of these
# requires an explicit human (code-owner) review before it can merge, even when CI is green and auto-merge
# is enabled. This is the enforcement for audit gate 12: THE AGENT MUST NOT be able to weaken its own
# safety controls without a human review path. Everything NOT listed here can follow the normal flow.
#
# NOTE: this is only a hard gate against the agent once (a) branch protection has
# "Require review from Code Owners" enabled AND (b) the agent runs under a scoped identity that is NOT an
# admin and NOT the code owner (so it cannot approve its own PR or bypass as admin). Until then it documents
# intent and gates non-admin contributors. See docs/ai-bridge-responder.md "Controller-owned gates".

# CI / CD and the merge gate itself
/.github/                       @hgbobia-zoe

# Deploy + runtime infrastructure
/Dockerfile                     @hgbobia-zoe
/fly.toml                       @hgbobia-zoe

# Test configuration (disabling/weakening tests must be reviewed)
/vitest.config.ts               @hgbobia-zoe

# Authentication & authorization
/src/lib/auth/                  @hgbobia-zoe

# The execution gate (what an approved action is allowed to do) and the AI provider seam
/src/lib/aiorg/approvals.ts     @hgbobia-zoe
/src/lib/ai/provider.ts         @hgbobia-zoe

# The autonomous loop's own control surface (sessions, requests backlog, bridge endpoints, the contract)
/src/lib/ai/sessions.ts         @hgbobia-zoe
/src/lib/ai/requests.ts         @hgbobia-zoe
/src/lib/ai/improvement/        @hgbobia-zoe
/src/app/api/ai/bridge/         @hgbobia-zoe
/src/app/api/ai/requests/       @hgbobia-zoe
/docs/ai-bridge-responder.md    @hgbobia-zoe
